      "snippet": {
        "text": "Additionally, it is time-consuming, unreliable, and may not account for contextual factors that influence instructional effectiveness or capture the full scope of teaching practices. Even so, T-KPI forms can contribute to a more comprehensive understanding of teacher performance when used thoughtfully and in conjunction with other evaluation methods [41]. \n\nThe manual analysis of teaching process video recordings is an effective method for evaluating teacher performance by capturing a comprehensive view of teaching practices, including instructional strategies, classroom management techniques, and interactions with students in a non-intrusive way. Furthermore, it provides evaluators with a wealth of data that can be used to assess teaching effectiveness as well as identify areas that require improvement. Despite this, there are challenges regarding video review, such as its time-consuming nature and the need to ensure that data is evaluated objectively and reliably by trained evaluators. Additionally, video recordings must be carefully managed in terms of privacy concerns and ethical considerations [42]. \n\nThe emergence of AI technology presents new opportunities to improve teacher evaluation, as it represents a transformational approach to assessing educational performance. With AI, a vast amount of information can be analyzed from a variety of sources, such as classroom interactions, student performance metrics, and instructional materials, to provide a more complete understanding of teaching effectiveness. Through AI algorithms, educators' strengths and areas for improvement can be evaluated more accurately and objectively through the observation of patterns in their teaching methods and student engagement levels. Furthermore, AI-driven evaluations can provide teachers with immediate feedback that allows them to adapt their instructional practices to better meet the needs of their students [43]. However, ensuring data privacy, addressing algorithmic bias, and maintaining the interpretability of AI-generated assessments remain pressing concerns. Despite this, ongoing research suggests that the integration of AI into teacher performance evaluations may result in an enhanced level of quality and fairness in assessments [44]. \n\nOverall, T-KPI analysis is essential for enhancing educational outcomes, accountability, professional growth, and evidence-based decision-making [28,45]. Moreover, there are five common types of T-KPIs: (a) student achievement, (b) instructional quality, (c) professional development and growth, (d) collaboration and communication, and (e) classroom environment.",
