rners and transfer to the teachers that their learning is not dominant to the procedure and that they are merely conduits for change. It is in this complex context that policymakers and external providers of PD need to improve and implement effective programs that consider the specific needs of individual schools and two learner groups: teachers and primary children, Petrie & Mcgee (2012).",
