      "snippet": {
        "text": "With the result orientation of various influencing factors, educators should help students smoothly use relevant AI tools to be more confident in using these technologies in the classroom. Through the education and practice of AI technology, students can use AI chatbots for autonomous learning, thus positively impacting language learning. \n\nEducators can use AI chatbots to conduct teaching activities in real classroom settings. Real-life situations are simulated through character dialogue tasks, such as ordering food in restaurants and asking for directions in tourism. Teachers can provide simple dialogue exercises for students with weaker foundations, tailored to their language levels, to improve their oral English skills. More complex scene dialogue tasks are designed for students with higher English proficiency, enabling personalized learning path customization. In the teaching process, educators should fully leverage the instant feedback function of AI chatbots to help students identify problems in real-time and improve their language expression. Additionally, students' learning feedback can be regularly collected through classroom quizzes or questionnaires. Educators should adjust the teaching plan based on students' needs to help them achieve their learning goals more effectively.",
