        "text": "Artificial intelligence (AI) has grown exponentially in recent years, with the advent of OpenAI's ChatGPT marking a new era of generative AI. This technology has greatly expanded human potential and boosted productivity. Generative AI is now embedded in everyday applications, from search engines and chatbots to office tools and specialized software. \n\nIn education, educators are increasingly receptive to AI technologies. While exploring ways to harness the power of AI, educational technology (EdTech) vendors have developed a wide range of AI products, such as writing assistants (e.g., [8]), study tools in e-textbooks (e.g., [22]), lesson planning toolsets for teachers (e.g., [15]), and AI-assisted grading applications (e.g., [7]). As Chan and Hu [4] and Montalvo [16] noted, generative AI is reshaping education by fostering more responsive and personalized learning experiences. Additionally, generative AI possesses great potential for providing instant feedback, facilitating language learning, and increasing educators' efficiency by streamlining content preparation [11,20].",
