        "text": "Figure 1 shows the framework for applying generative artificial intelligence applications such as ChatGPT, Google Bard, and others. As stated in the framework, generative artificial intelligence applications are developed based on large language models. Generative artificial intelligence applications generate responses to human input by analyzing the context and understanding the content. To guarantee the quality and credibility of the findings, this review included only articles from reputable journals. Studies that focused on AI development without any relation to education, or those that discussed AI in a theoretical manner without demonstrating practical applications in educational settings, were excluded. Similarly, research addressing general technological advancements without specifically focusing on AI's role in education fell outside the scope of this review. \n\nTo maintain academic rigor and uphold the integrity of the review, additional exclusion criteria were established. Articles that lacked sufficient methodological or analytical depth, did not meet necessary academic standards, or were published outside the last five years were excluded.",
