      "snippet": {
        "text": "A significant body of research aims to explore how AI can be utilized in education, reflecting a heightened interest in using AI for educational purposes within the academic community [6]. Traditional methods of evaluating teachers through T-KPI tools are recognized as subjective, time-consuming, costly, and inefficient. The advent of AI technology presents promising prospects for enhancing teacher evaluation practice in schools. AI-based systems offer the potential to deliver objective and reliable evaluations, facilitating the identification of areas requiring improvement and contributing to the overall improvement of the education provided to students [7]. \n\nDespite the global attention that AI technology has received from researchers and educators, there appears to be a notable gap in existing research. To the best of our knowledge, no research has focused on teacher performance evaluation considering overall evaluation elements to estimate an ultimate performance automatically.",
