      "snippet": {
        "text": "Moreover, there are five common types of T-KPIs: (a) student achievement, (b) instructional quality, (c) professional development and growth, (d) collaboration and communication, and (e) classroom environment. AI-based systems can provide objective and reliable evaluations, helping to identify areas that need improvement and enhance the quality of education offered to students [28]. \n\nThis article introduces an experimental analytic study of the T-KPIs adopted in Saudi Arabia. It also proposes a comprehensive weighted index that incorporates all the T-KPI criteria by analyzing them thoroughly. The study explores available evaluation data sources, identifies potential AI applications for each criterion, and introduces a prototype design of the AI-based teacher evaluation system. Moreover, it presents two algorithms: an overall teacher performance evaluation and an algorithm for the element under study, as we will illustrate later. The weights of the evaluation elements (Criteria) adopted in the evaluation system were derived from our conducted study, where we tested our hypothesis to acquire the actual weights. Moreover, the article extensively analyzes the elements under study to build our model accordingly going forward. Eventually, the proposed evaluation index system will help to carry out a reliable decision objectively by considering several weighted evaluation elements currently used by educational supervisors and principals. \n\nThe rest of this article is organized as follows. Section 2 demonstrates the rationale of the study. The related works are reviewed in Sect. 3. Section 4 introduces the material and methods of study. The results, discussion, and conclusion are illustrated in Sects. 5, 6, and 7 respectively.",
