        "text": "Generative AI emerges as a transformative tool in the educational sector, offering a broad spectrum of support functions beyond traditional teaching methodologies. Its application ranges from easing administrative burdens to enriching curriculum development, allowing educators to devote more attention to the pedagogical core of teaching and learning [23], [38]. This technology automates tedious queries and fosters educational content creation, streamlining communication and instructional material development [7]. Furthermore, its capabilities as an instructional aide manifest through its ability to generate tailored instructional content, as an online tutor, and leverage smartphones and Internet of Things (IoT) gadgets to make education more accessible and interactive. This versatility improves the learning experience by facilitating collaborative group work and allowing education to be more adaptive and personalized [39]. It also promotes innovative teaching methods by introducing novel pedagogical strategies that leverage GAI capabilities [2]. Its support is also crucial for promoting mental well-being and preparing educators and students with the skills necessary to navigate mental health challenges [40]. GAI tools and chatbots also play a vital role in lesson planning, test creation, and the development of sample solutions, thus improving teaching efficiency [41], [42]. Moreover, generative AI tools support instructors in integrating technology into the classroom, offering a platform for conducting workshops and discussions centered around responses generated by them. This facilitates a deeper understanding of how AI can be used to improve teaching and learning outcomes [43].",
