      "snippet": {
        "text": "The integration of AI tools, such as ChatGPT and GitHub Copilot, has significantly enhanced learning outcomes in introductory programming courses. Our systematic review and meta-analysis provides compelling evidence that AI-powered tools contribute to higher exam scores, improved computer programming proficiency, increased task completion rates, and greater student engagement. By synthesising data from 32 controlled studies, our findings demonstrate that students who utilised AI tools consistently outperformed those relying solely on traditional instructional methods, completing tasks more efficiently and producing higher-quality code. While AI tools, on average, had a positive effect on learning outcomes, variations between studies suggest that factors such as tool design, student characteristics, and implementation quality may influence their effectiveness. Addressing these factors through optimised instructional strategies can enhance scalability and accessibility, further improving the impact of AI in computer programming education. \n\nDespite these positive outcomes, substantial heterogeneity (I 2 = 88%) was observed, indicating that AI effectiveness depends on various contextual factors, including course design, AI functionality, and student interaction. While AI tools offer transformative potential, their integration into computer programming education requires carefully designed pedagogical strategies to maximise benefits while mitigating risks, such as over-reliance on automation and diminished problem-solving skills. \n\nFuture research should focus on optimising AI-assisted learning through adaptive models, personalised AI tutoring systems, and hybrid approaches that blend AI support with traditional instruction. In addition, addressing ethical concerns, including academic integrity and algorithmic bias, is essential to ensuring equitable and responsible AI use in education. \n\nIn conclusion, AI-driven learning tools are redefining computer programming education by offering personalised, efficient, and interactive learning experiences. However, their widespread adoption must be supported by evidence-based instructional strategies and continuous evaluation to sustain their effectiveness across diverse educational settings. By refining AI integration approaches, educators and institutions can harness AI's full potential to enhance student learning while fostering critical thinking and independent problem-solving skills. Accuracy: How well the explanation described the code's functionality. Understandability: Ease of comprehending the explanation. Length: Whether the explanation was considered ideal in length. Thematic Analysis: Students' perceptions of what makes a good explanation (e.g., detailed, line-by-line descriptions).",
