      "snippet": {
        "text": "Automated Essay Scoring The task of Automated Essay Scoring (AES) (Page, 1966), aims to reduce human grading effort and improve consistency in writing assessment. Most widely used AES benchmarks consist of essays written to standardized prompts in general-domain language. These essays are typically manually annotated with a holistic score, complemented by scores for a small set of assessment criteria (e.g., content, organization, language) (Mathias and Bhattacharyya, 2018;Gaudeau, 2025;Li and Ng, 2024;Xue et al., 2021;Crossley et al., 2023;Ishikawa, 2023). Importantly, these benchmarks do not include human feedback, revisions, or feedback assessment scores. Feedback datasets. A small number of resources connect student writing with feedback and/or revision. ArgRewrite links multiple drafts of student argumentative essays, annotates revision purposes, and also includes instructor feedback (Zhang et al., 2017;Kashefi et al., 2022). Pilan et al. (2020) release a teacher-feedback dataset pairing original and revised student sentences with comments and tags for a targeted error type, enabling analyses of how feedback relates to revision outcomes. For peer feedback, Rietsche et al. (2022) collect peer reviews written by Master's students and annotate for specificity and perceived helpfulness. However, existing datasets lack (i) passage-anchored inline comments tied to draft spans, (ii) role-separated peer and instructor feedback, and (iii) criterionlevel assessment scores on the text to be assessed and the feedback. Exposía addresses these gaps by capturing a full draft→feedback→revision work- flow with peer and instructor feedback. LLM-based scoring and transfer to peer review Recent work evaluates LLMs as scorers and emphasizes that educational use requires evidence beyond accuracy (Pack et al., 2024;Huang and Wilson, 2025). Exposía complements this line of work, by enabling fine-grained exposé and feedback assessment with LLMs and interpreting LLM-human alignment relative to human agreement (Section 6).",
