      "snippet": {
        "text": "Technology has been the applications used to achieve goals faster and in more simplified manners. Since technology literacy is at the core of 21 st century skills (Voogt & Roblin, 2010), school districts are constantly changing and improving the ways teachers communicate with parents (Tyson, 2020). The new trend in digital communication has replaced the traditional use of communicating through paper, so much that school districts now encourage parent-teacher communication through technology (Ho et al., 2013;Tyson, 2020). For family-school partnerships to fully benefit from technology, both parents and teachers must be willing to embrace technology as a communication tool (Rogers & Wright, 2008). \n\nThere are four major types of communication: verbal, non-verbal, written, and visual (Indeed Career Guide, 2021). Teachers and parents could exchange information through any of these ways of communication. In this paper, focus will be on verbal communication; how English-speaking teachers can verbally communicate (converse) effectively with non-English parents. There are two possible means, among others, that teachers use when they need the service of speech translation -human interpreters and translation apps. Few human interpreters were already mentioned: teacher-interpreters, student-interpreters and hired interpreters (e.g., Voiance). Two speech translation apps were also mentioned: Google Translate and Microsoft Translator. Some essential benefits of translation apps over human interpreters make the software appealing for speech translation (Table 4). Translation service by hired interpreters is very expensive. Users do not need to have the knowledge of language of their guests. \n\nInterpreters need to have good knowledge of the language invited to interpret. \n\nNo risk of divulging confidential reports. \n\nTeachers feel reluctant to use students as interpreters for sensitive discussions about other students. Single translation app can be used to hold a multilanguage conference of speakers of more than ten different languages at a time. \n\nHumans can only interpret few languages at a time. Hired interpreters are specialized in one or two languages. \n\nSources: Microsoft Corporation (2021); Google Liability Limited Company (2021); Voiance (2021) Based on the data collected, 42.9% (6 out of 14) surveyed and interviewed teachers favored technology or speech translation apps as suitable tools for translating speech conversations with non-English parents.",
